WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.110
- All right,(indistinct) scouring the web

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:04.070
to find stories that
might brighten your day.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.450
This Is What I'm Liking.

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:07.471
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.471 --> 00:00:08.970
(Audience applauds)

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.810
Earlier we met LA's
first female Fire Chief.

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:14.770
She told us that she's often
come across dire situations

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:18.320
off duty and that her training
immediately kicks into gear.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.800
And that's what happened
to Pasadena Fire Captain

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:24.430
last month just as he was about
to head out to a Rams game,

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:25.945
he saw go Rams.

00:00:25.945 --> 00:00:28.860
(indistinct) he saw smoke
billowing in his neighborhood.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:30.210
So he sprung into action,

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.670
ultimately rescuing a
woman from the second floor

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.020
along with her dog.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:35.290
We have him on the line right now.

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:37.830
So everybody say hi to
Captain William Basulto

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:41.332
who watches on NBC4 Los Angeles at two.

00:00:41.332 --> 00:00:42.504
(audience applauds)

00:00:42.504 --> 00:00:44.430
- Hello hello how you doing?

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:45.874
Hi Kelly. Thanks for having me.

00:00:45.874 --> 00:00:49.850
- Hi. So you're a hero, so
thank you for being that.

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:51.519
First of all, that was awesome.

00:00:51.519 --> 00:00:52.593
(audience applauds)

00:00:52.593 --> 00:00:54.810
- (indistinct) thank you very,
very much. I appreciate it.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:55.970
- Take us back to that day.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:57.340
What was happening?

00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:58.470
- Well, it was a great day.

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:00.500
My father and I and son
were supposed to head out

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.020
to the NFC Championship Game.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:04.440
We're gonna tailgate have a great old time

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.580
but while we're packing
the car and getting ready,

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:09.690
my father spotted a
fire across the street.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:10.523
He pointed out.

00:01:10.523 --> 00:01:11.840
I said, well, let me go see if I can help.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:13.020
Headed over there

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:16.210
and I found a well
involved two story units

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:18.110
with my community members
running over there

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:19.740
with garden hoses and extinguishers.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:21.380
So I got to direct them on what to do.

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:23.200
Break that window, put it there.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:26.140
And at that point they
tell me somebody's trapped.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:27.050
I look to the left.

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:30.810
I see a lady's screen
door facing gets a screen

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:32.950
trapped in the second
floor with heavy smoke.

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:34.450
I called out for a ladder.

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:36.030
They brought me a small ladder at first.

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:39.090
I was only able to reach
up to about my about here

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:40.150
and tell her stay low.

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:41.110
I'll take care of you.

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:42.770
I called out for another ladder.

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:44.430
I didn't hear any sirens.

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:46.120
So I called for 911.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:48.170
And as I got off the phone with 911

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:51.120
to tell 'em we have a fire,
they brought me a second ladder.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:54.500
I was able to throw it ladder
rescue the lady and her dog.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:56.560
At that point, the fire
department showed up

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:59.390
and I was able to give the
Fire captain some lingo

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:01.350
on what I did and what I was doing.

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:04.850
And he looked at me like, who
is this Rams fan in Rams gear,

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:06.428
speaking the fire department lingo.

00:02:06.428 --> 00:02:08.200
- (laughs)I love that.

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:09.460
So was the woman okay?

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:10.363
Was her dog okay?

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:12.430
- The dog survived.

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:14.950
The woman went to the hospital,
was there for a few days

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:16.300
a lot of smoke inhalation.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:17.440
She was out feeling better

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:20.210
but the next day I did
get to meet the family,

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:24.730
the daughter, the father, her
father, and the daughter cried

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:26.640
in my arms and thanked me
for saving their mother.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:27.730
But they were really distraught

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:29.050
that they had lost their home.

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:30.560
But at that point, the
committee had set up a GoFundMe

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:32.730
and everybody's been contributing to it.

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:33.607
- Oh, that's amazing.

00:02:33.607 --> 00:02:34.970
(audience applauds)

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:37.228
Thank you so much Captain Basulto

00:02:37.228 --> 00:02:38.548
I'm liking your post right know alright.

00:02:38.548 --> 00:02:40.375
(audience applauds)

00:02:40.375 --> 00:02:41.725
- Thank you, thank you.

00:02:41.725 --> 00:02:42.558
- And that's not all,

00:02:42.558 --> 00:02:44.790
our seasonal partner
Pilot Pen Makers of G2

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.440
that Go To Pen Of The Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:49.030
wanna honor ultimate
overachievers just like you, sir.

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:51.070
So in your name, they're
gonna write a check

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:53.640
for a $ 1000 to help the
family who lost their home

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:54.760
in the fire.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:55.965
- Thank you thank you thank you so much.

00:02:55.965 --> 00:02:57.476
- Thank you so much sir.

